# ldr pc, [sp], #4 is a return. The saved lr was replaced with 0x4001, so the return check
# stops it at the ldr (BASE+4) with MT_TRAP_BAD_RETURN; the post-index has written sp back.
title: ldr pc, [sp], #4 to an address other than the entry lr stops with MT_TRAP_BAD_RETURN
ref: A8.8 LDR (immediate, Thumb) T4 with Rt = 15 (post-indexed): LoadWritePC(); ADR 0014: returns are C returns, checked against the entry lr

[code]
00b5        push {lr}
0090        str r0, [sp]
5df804fb    ldr pc, [sp], #4

[in]
r0 = 0x4001

[out]
trap = bad_return BASE+4 0x4001
word SP0-4 = 0x4001
